tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-133-a-swap-certain-only-where-its-word-is-right.hero:23:1: error[reserved_word]: `include` is not a word in this language — a C header is named by an `extern` group, with the signatures it declares indented below it: `extern "stdio.h"`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-133-a-swap-certain-only-where-its-word-is-right.hero:25:1: error[reserved_word]: `switch` is not a word in this language — `match` is an expression, written inside a body over the value it matches, with its arms below: `y = match x`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-133-a-swap-certain-only-where-its-word-is-right.hero:27:1: error[reserved_word]: `int` is not a word in this language — an integer type says its width, `i64`, and a type is written where a type goes: after a name and `:`, or after `->`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-133-a-swap-certain-only-where-its-word-is-right.hero:30:5: error[reserved_word]: `enum` is not a word in this language — an `extern` group holds no `variant`: a C enumeration's values are the group's `constant`s, one per line: `constant MODE_A: i32`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-133-a-swap-certain-only-where-its-word-is-right.hero:34:18: error[reserved_word]: `struct` is not a word in this language — a type names the `record` itself: `p: Point`
